Subject: Retain physically stopped native SDK contexts through final power removal
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

The native SDK cannot destroy live original C++ stacks as Wii context removal
would. Mark only the original final power-off boundary after its real shutdown
callbacks and mask, immediately before unchanged KillThreads. The host accepts
only genuinely parked, unborrowed, lock-free native waits; their cancelled source
records retain the original semantics while native frames stay alive until the
configured process power removal. No normal completion, game cleanup or source
shutdown message is invented. Other shutdown events retain their existing path.

diff --git a/src/RVL_SDK/os/OSReset.c b/src/RVL_SDK/os/OSReset.c
index 77ef427..cb016fb 100644
--- a/src/RVL_SDK/os/OSReset.c
+++ b/src/RVL_SDK/os/OSReset.c
@@ -194,6 +194,11 @@ void __OSShutdownDevices(u32 event) {
         __PADDisableRecalibration(disableRecalibration);
     }
 
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+    if (event == OS_SHUTDOWN_SHUTDOWN) {
+        ChargedNativeBeginThreadPowerRemoval();
+    }
+#endif
     KillThreads();
 }
 
